     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended adult dose of amlodipine is 10 mg once daily. Usual doses are 2.5\u201310 mg. 50 mg is five times the maximum and could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged shock. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that. It may be a typo, for example 5 mg.\n\n2. **You aren't a clinician.** Medication orders need to come from a licensed prescriber, or be verified by one. I can't confirm that this order is authorized.\n\nIf a prescriber wants this entered, ask them to confirm the intended dose. If it is 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily, I can enter it once they or you confirm. If they really do intend 50 mg, they should enter and document it themselves. Pharmacy would also need to verify it."
      }
